# Odin build artifacts.
#
# `odin` names a binary after the directory it builds, and the name moves
# depending on how you invoke the compiler:
#
#   odin run  loops       -> loops/looping   (binary lands inside the target dir)
#   odin build loops      -> ./loops.bin     (binary lands in the CWD)
#   odin build .          -> ./<name of CWD> (when run from inside a dir)
#   odin build loops/x.odin -> loops/loops    (name of the source file's dir)
#
# A bare `loops` pattern would also match the loops/ *source* directory, which
# makes git skip the whole tree and hide every .odin file inside it. So the
# binary names are anchored to full paths below.
#
# Add a new pair of lines whenever you add a new topic directory.
*.bin
*.exe

/constants/constants
/dynamics/dynamics
/greeting/greeting
/hello/hello
/loops/looping
/loops/loops

# `odin build .` from the repo root.
/odin-lang-study

.DS_Store